      "text": "Reporting as of 10:49 EST on 5 November 2026.\n\nJobs watch: weaker hiring can cut both ways for US stocks\n\nWhy it matters: Lower Treasury yields could support equity valuations if investors also lower the rate they use to value future profits.\n\nContext: Continued hiring, stable unemployment and moderating wage growth would fit orderly cooling. Rising unemployment and further downward revisions would strengthen the growth-risk interpretation.\n\nRead the full brief: https://capitalchronicle.substack.com/p/jobs-watch-weaker-hiring-can-cut\n\nAnalysis, not financial advice. Readers decide whether to trade.\n\nCapital Chronicle may hold positions in the markets it covers.\n\nSource: BLS."
